  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The spin only magnetic moment of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Mn</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> complexes is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Nearest integer)</p><p>(Given atomic number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A spin-only magnetic moment occurs when an electron rotates on its own axis and generates a magnetic field.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mi>BM</mi></math><br />Here, n is the number of unpaired electrons.<br />The unit for a spin-only magnetic moment is the Bohr magneton (BM).</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Mn</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>91</mn><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
